course: dictionary
lesson: 209
title: Ale and other drinks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ale is a kind of beer. It is often darker or stronger than other beers, and it is made with malted barley. «Medieval people drank weak ale, but they also drank water from wells and springs.» In the Middle Ages, people often drank ale because water could be unsafe.
explain: Old stories often set ale in inns and taverns, where travellers stopped to eat and drink. «The Rat warms up some ale with spices, as people did in those days, and the field-mice sip and cough and laugh.» Warming ale with spices makes it mulled ale.
explain: Be careful: ginger ale is a fizzy soft drink with no alcohol, even though it has the word ale in its name. Ale can also mean any beer, which is an old-fashioned use. Look at the words around it to work out which meaning fits.
fact: Ale is a kind of beer, often darker or stronger, made with malted barley.
fact: In an old-fashioned way, «ale» can mean any beer.
fact: In the Middle Ages, people often drank ale because water could be unsafe.
fact: Mulled ale is beer warmed with spices.
fact: Ginger ale is a fizzy soft drink with no alcohol.
exercise: What is ale? | A fizzy soft drink with no alcohol | A type of bread baked in an oven | *A kind of beer, often darker or stronger, made with malted barley | A small glass for drinking water
exercise: «Medieval people drank weak ale, but they also drank water from wells and springs.» Why did people in the Middle Ages often drink ale? | *Water could be unsafe | Ale tasted of ginger | Water was too expensive to buy | Ale was only for children
exercise: Ginger ale is a fizzy soft drink. Does it contain alcohol? | Yes, it is always very strong | *No, it has no alcohol | It depends on how much ginger is in it | Yes, it is a kind of beer
test: The Rat says, «Now we shall be able to mull some ale!» What does mulled ale mean? | Ale that is only for children | Ale with no barley in it | Ale kept cold in a well | *Ale warmed with spices
test: «The mice sip and cough, for a little mulled ale goes a long way.» What does this suggest about mulled ale? | It tastes of ginger only | It is so weak you need a lot of it | *It is strong, so a little goes a long way | It is only water with spices
exam: A pupil says ginger ale is a kind of beer. Is she right? | Yes, it is darker and stronger than other beers | *No, it is a fizzy soft drink with no alcohol | Only in old stories | Yes, because it has ale in its name
